{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_31d1ad6ebb0ad4e089bf2979226464e68b3a5f0d67edf8f811e74a9951c6193d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two skills are provided: /prd for generating Product Requirements Documents and /ralph for converting PRDs to prd.json, installable via Amp config, the Claude skills directory, or a Claude Code marketplace plugin."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4412202e98be0eb0f48be3c6cf6b8e5c85a79d03521ae77972a26e0ec3eb67d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Key files include ralph.sh (the bash loop), prompt.md and CLAUDE.md prompt templates, prd.json task list, progress.txt, skills/prd and skills/ralph, and a .claude-plugin manifest."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4456223d7175bb2ae9491440dee1bedabe78226ebae884a9882ebb095a7911b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"When all stories have passes:true, Ralph outputs <promise>COMPLETE</promise> and the loop exits."},{"claim_ids":["clm_47b5afd707d9cc986839d139be55dbfbcc73b24ae3b0cb0f0a93e083f74c254c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A recommended Amp auto-handoff setting (context 90) enables automatic handoff when context fills, letting Ralph handle stories larger than one context window."},{"claim_ids":["clm_54a1a0f5098ee00a2e3990252799d74d4bb67491bccd573b68936b6dec47101c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each loop iteration creates a feature branch from the PRD branchName, picks the highest-priority story with passes:false, implements it, runs quality checks, commits, marks it passes:true, and repeats until done or max iterations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57f12a42be43f6b3e1b258a72291259eaf9ad55766b65f8c964fa999e4191098"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Frontend stories' acceptance criteria must include browser verification via the dev-browser skill, which Ralph uses to navigate and confirm UI changes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f58b84e7fbc4706fa22097cb989b448fad63a8691342c2d6f7c16125910eb4c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites are one installed and authenticated AI coding tool (Amp CLI default or Claude Code), jq, and a git repository for the project."},{"claim_ids":["clm_924725008f8e5bf781aa2703f913c55af8ca337ae3a13f763bc365c534cab01e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The only memory between iterations is git history, the append-only progress.txt learnings file, and prd.json story status."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a7896f2edf35bc19945f1729418be774036f20f093564a57f0b34383ae9bdd7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ralph runs AI coding tools (Amp or Claude Code) repeatedly until all PRD items are complete; each iteration is a fresh instance with clean context."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b0970ae2289f347e3b740d6edfbef7738e057d1b2e0e8e5d8e9ae6be44cc5ae6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"PRD items are intentionally kept small enough to finish in one context window, since oversized tasks exhaust context and yield poor code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d9a0a1184b1fdee9bb9995fea7c7bef8b13ba613e9fac7b34c39458be7537488"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ralph.sh accepts an optional max_iterations argument and a --tool flag selecting amp (the default) or claude; the default iteration count is 10."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7d31f86b5f5fdba0b3543e9ddc5bffb9fc17e7209f6d85eed4a9deed025747b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ralph automatically archives previous runs when a new feature with a different branchName starts, saving them under archive/YYYY-MM-DD-feature-name/."}],"claim_ids":["clm_31d1ad6ebb0ad4e089bf2979226464e68b3a5f0d67edf8f811e74a9951c6193d","clm_4412202e98be0eb0f48be3c6cf6b8e5c85a79d03521ae77972a26e0ec3eb67d1","clm_4456223d7175bb2ae9491440dee1bedabe78226ebae884a9882ebb095a7911b4","clm_47b5afd707d9cc986839d139be55dbfbcc73b24ae3b0cb0f0a93e083f74c254c","clm_54a1a0f5098ee00a2e3990252799d74d4bb67491bccd573b68936b6dec47101c","clm_57f12a42be43f6b3e1b258a72291259eaf9ad55766b65f8c964fa999e4191098","clm_8f58b84e7fbc4706fa22097cb989b448fad63a8691342c2d6f7c16125910eb4c","clm_924725008f8e5bf781aa2703f913c55af8ca337ae3a13f763bc365c534cab01e","clm_9a7896f2edf35bc19945f1729418be774036f20f093564a57